    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0530" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg524"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Salisbury to Consul
                    Cusack-Smith</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegraphic, P.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-05T16:30:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                                1891–430p.m</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Navigator Islands, December 5; confidential, 81; section
                    1.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">No. 1.</p>
                <p>Yon should unite with the German consul in urging the Samoan Government to take
                    measures in accordance with the request of the municipal council of the 3d June
                    and of the 24th July last respecting the currency question.</p>
                <p>Her Majesty’s minister at Washington will be instructed to urge the U. S.
                    Government to issue similar directions to the American consul.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
